class.description:
Reached through [member NetwEntity.simulation]. Each peer runs the entity in one [member mode], which decides whether [member step] runs and whether the body is frozen. A game sets the members below and reads [member mode].
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
func _init() -> void:
    var entity := Netw.configure_entity(self)
    entity.simulation.bodies = [^"Sphere"]
    entity.simulation.replicas = NetwSimulationHandle.REPLICAS_ACTIVE

func _network_tick(delta: float, tick: int, is_fresh: bool) -> void:
    if is_fresh:
        steer(delta)
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
public Car()
{
    var entity = Netw.ConfigureEntity(this);
    entity.Simulation.Bodies = new Godot.Collections.Array { new NodePath("Sphere") };
    entity.Simulation.Replicas = NetwSimulationHandle.ReplicasEnum.Active;
    entity.Simulation.Step = Callable.From<double, long, bool>(Step);
}

private void Step(double delta, long tick, bool isFresh)
{
    if (isFresh)
        Steer(delta);
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
An entity is simulated once it sets or calls anything here, declares [member NetwPredictionHandle.archetype], or has a [RigidBody2D] or [RigidBody3D] root drawn by [member NetwEntity.interpolation]. Other entities stay [constant MODE_NONE].

[b]Modes[/b]
The peer with authority over the entity runs it as [constant MODE_AUTHORITY], and a client predicting it runs it as [constant MODE_PREDICT]. Every other copy is a frozen [constant MODE_PROXY], unless [member replicas] or a selection makes it [constant MODE_ACTIVE].

[b]Selection[/b]
While this entity runs here as [constant MODE_AUTHORITY] or [constant MODE_PREDICT], it can pick other entities to run here as [constant MODE_ACTIVE]. [method simulate] names one. [method simulate_nearest], [method simulate_within] and [method simulate_all] set a policy, and each call replaces the last.
[codeblock]
func _ready() -> void:
    entity.simulation.simulate(ball)
    entity.simulation.simulate_nearest(2, &"arena")
[/codeblock]
